# Every variable the Social Manager reads, and nothing else.
#
#   cp .env.example .env        # .env is gitignored; this file never holds a value
#
# Leave a line empty to leave that capability off: an empty variable is the same as
# an absent one, and the connectors then explain what is missing instead of failing.
# In draft mode (the default) an empty file is a complete, working configuration.
#
# Nothing in this repository is allowed to print these values: the CLI's
# ``token-check``, the dashboard's *Social Accounts* page and ``status`` show the
# variable *name*, whether it is set, and a one-way fingerprint.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- behaviour
# Comma-separated ``section.field=value`` overrides applied on top of the config file.
# This is how the container changes behaviour without a second YAML file, and it is
# the only switch that turns the autonomy up:
#
#   SOCIAL_OVERRIDES=autonomy.mode=controlled
#
# The autonomy levels are  draft | controlled | advanced  (the default is draft).
#   draft       the AI writes drafts and replies; nothing is published
#   controlled  ordinary content that passes the policy engine publishes itself;
#               sensitive items wait for an approval
#   advanced    the same, plus the calendar and the reports adapt on their own
#
# A typo'd key is reported rather than ignored: ``doctor`` lists it under
# ``unknown_keys``.  An override can never loosen the policy engine - its limits are
# read from the config, whose defaults are the conservative ones.
SOCIAL_OVERRIDES=

# Path to the YAML configuration.  The image sets SOCIAL_CONFIG=/app/social.yaml and
# that file does not have to exist: without it, the documented defaults are used.
# SOCIAL_CONFIG=/app/social.yaml

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- GitHub (read-only)
# Optional.  A public repository is read anonymously at 60 requests/hour; a token
# raises that to 5,000 and is the only way to see Discussions.  A classic token with
# exactly ``public_repo`` (or a fine-grained token with, at most, Contents: read,
# Issues: read, Discussions: read) is enough - the connector never writes.
SOCIAL_GITHUB_TOKEN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- X (Twitter)
# OAuth 2.0 with user context.  The app setup and the required scopes
# (tweet.read, tweet.write, users.read, media.write, offline.access) are in
# docs/SOCIAL-MANAGER.md; ``refresh_token`` is what keeps a long-running worker alive.
SOCIAL_X_CLIENT_ID=
SOCIAL_X_CLIENT_SECRET=
SOCIAL_X_ACCESS_TOKEN=
SOCIAL_X_REFRESH_TOKEN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Instagram
# Instagram Graph API.  ``SOCIAL_IG_ACCESS_TOKEN`` needs instagram_business_basic +
# instagram_business_content_publish on a professional account; the app secret is
# used for the appsecret_proof on every call.
SOCIAL_IG_ACCESS_TOKEN=
SOCIAL_IG_APP_SECRET=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- LLM (optional)
# A local Ollama needs no key.  The remote provider is used only when it is both
# explicitly allowed in the config (llm.allow_remote_fallback) and configured here;
# with neither, the deterministic templates write the drafts and say so.
SOCIAL_LLM_API_KEY=
SOCIAL_LLM_REMOTE_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- dashboard
# Required to bind anything other than loopback.  At least 8 characters; it is stored
# only as a hash, in the state directory, and never in this file's history.
SOCIAL_DASHBOARD_PASSWORD=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- notifications (optional)
# Both variables must be set for notifications to be sent; notifications are off by default.
SOCIAL_TELEGRAM_TOKEN=
SOCIAL_TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- worker loop (compose only)
# Read by the ``worker`` service in docker-compose.yml; the CLI ignores them.
# SOCIAL_TICK_LIVE=0          # 1 = tick --live, i.e. really publish when policy allows
# SOCIAL_TICK_SECONDS=300     # pause between ticks
# SOCIAL_TICK_LIMIT=5         # jobs leased per tick
